# Project-specific read-only binds, on top of ~/.config/scoder/sandbox/readonly
# (which already covers .github/, .claude/, .gitignore and the usual lockfiles).

# The user R library, so installed packages (tidyverse, scoringRules,
# huxtable, btw, ...) load inside the sandbox.
$HOME/R

# The user-level R profile. It may not exist yet; the grant is still needed
# so it is bound if it is created later.
$HOME/.Rprofile


# The `loom` CLI (for the using-loom-cli / creating-a-loom-workflow skills).
# Chain: ~/.local/bin/loom -> ~/.bun/bin/loom -> ~/.bun/install/global (where
# `bun link` registers the package) -> the checkout it was linked from, so the
# whole ~/.bun tree is granted. The bun runtime itself is /usr/local/bin/bun.
# loom writes its DuckDB graph to design/.loom/ inside the project, which is
# already read-write.
$HOME/.local/bin/loom
$HOME/.bun
$HOME/Git/loom-cli
